}, {
  "@id" : "https://github.com/tumelomodise/LFTDO#LivestockEvent",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "LivestockEvent  is the \"Outcome\" or \"Alert\" of the Livestock Indicators."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "LivestockEvent"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://github.com/tumelomodise/LFTDO#LivestockIndicator",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "LivestockIndicators satisfy the necessary and sufficient conditions to infer a different high-level LivestockEvent (e.g., TheftEvent), providing a clear audit trail from raw data to actionable alert."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "LivestockIndicator"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://github.com/tumelomodise/LFTDO#Location",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Locations are farmer area where the livestock are being kept is referred to as a Farm.It can be at an urban, rural, or semi-urban location, and may have pen and open fields that are fenced or unfenced. \n\nThe position of livestock within a farm location is constrained to date and time, and their behavior influences their movement. The livestock position within a location may be indicated with coordinates such as longitude and latitude, which are used to precisely determine the location of livestock within a farm area, as discussed by  (Symeonaki et al., 2020).\n\nRelationships:\n1.Location (e.g., a farm) has a specific time period(startTime and endTime) during which certain events or activities occurs.\n2.Location (e.g., a farm) has a specific geographical position defined by latitude and longitude coordinates."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "Location"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid463"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid464"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid465"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid466"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid467"
  } ]
