  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Referenced Ontology:\n1.Suckling = suckling behavior(ATOL:0000365)\"any measurable or observable beahvioral characteristic related to the intake of milk by a preweaning organism\"(Meunier-Salaün et. al,2015)\n2.Suckling indicates the baby of livestock sucking miik from their mother, it had different rates, and number of times it does in an hour/day. \n3. it may have a abnormal behaviour state based on decreased suckling rate, which could indicate a baby livestock is separated from its mother\n\nIn ATOL under: animal trait of livestock->animal welfare trait->psychoneuroendocrinological state trait->behaviour trait->ingestive behavior->suckling behavior"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@value" : "Suckling"
  } ],
