  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Livestock has belong to a specific type of species\n\"Livestock species are defined as domesticated farm animals, such as buffalo, chicken, sheep, goats, pigs, cattle, duck, camel, horse, mole, and turkey, primarily raised for labor, meat, eggs, milk, fur, leather, and wool. They play a crucial role in agriculture and contribute significantly to the livelihoods of farm families.\" https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/agricultural-and-biological-sciences/livestock-species"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
